<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Bavaria-Straubing</h1><p class="st-meta">1353 CE – 1429 CE · capital Straubing</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Wittelsbach inheritance that joined a Lower Bavarian duchy with the rich Low Country counties of Holland, Zeeland and Hainaut.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-iv-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Louis the Bavarian</a> his sons divided their lands, and in 1353 a further partition created Bavaria-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/straubing">Straubing</a> for William I and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-i-duke-of-bavaria">Albert I</a>, together with the counties of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-hainaut">Hainaut</a>, Holland and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-zeeland">Zeeland</a> inherited through their mother Margaret. Albert governed the whole inheritance from 1358, after his brother became insane.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dukes lived mostly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a> and governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/straubing">Straubing</a> through deputies, while in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holland">County of Holland</a> they were drawn into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hook-and-cod-wars">Hook and Cod</a> factional wars. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> they built the ducal castle at Straubing from 1356. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> plain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauboden">Gäuboden</a> around the town was among the most fertile farmland in Bavaria.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-duke-of-bavaria">William VI</a> died in 1417 his daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacqueline-countess-of-hainaut">Jacqueline of Hainaut</a> fought her uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-iii-duke-of-bavaria">John III</a> for the inheritance. John died in 1425, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a> passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Burgundy</a>, and in 1429 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/straubing">Straubing</a> lands were divided among the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-bavaria-munich">Duchy of Bavaria-Munich</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-bavaria-ingolstadt">Duchy of Bavaria-Ingolstadt</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-bavaria-landshut">Duchy of Bavaria-Landshut</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-bavaria-straubing.jpg" alt="Duchy of Bavaria-Straubing" width="320" height="315"><figcaption>Image: Lencer · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Bavaria-Straubing_-_Karte_Straubing-Holland.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1353 CE – 1429 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Straubing</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Albert I, William VI, John III</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bavarian German, Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Straubing-Holland, Bayern-Straubing</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1391&amp;focus=duchy-of-bavaria-straubing" aria-label="Duchy of Bavaria-Straubing on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4971 471 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Bavaria-Straubing lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5291 727L5282 737M5291 727L5269 749"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5282 737h0M5269 749h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5291 727h0"/><path clas